course: dictionary
lesson: 12409
title: A name with a history
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Cyril is a name. A name for a person is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter. «Cyril kicked the ball over the fence.» Cyril is the boy's first name, so he is a person, not an action or a thing.
explain: Names can be old and can come in and out of fashion. «Great-grandad was called Cyril, and many boys had that name in the early 1900s.» Today the name is less common, so you may meet it more in old family stories and history books.
explain: Some names belong to famous people from history. «Saint Cyril helped bring Christian faith and writing to many Slavic peoples.» When you meet Cyril, ask yourself: is this a person's name, or is it a word for something?
fact: Cyril is a man's first name.
fact: Names always start with a capital letter.
fact: Saint Cyril was a Christian missionary of the 800s who worked with his brother Methodius.
fact: The Cyrillic alphabet, used for languages such as Russian and Bulgarian, is named after Saint Cyril, though it was probably made by his followers.
fact: Cyril was popular as a name in Britain in the early 1900s and is less common now.
exercise: «Cyril kicked the ball over the fence.» What kind of word is Cyril here? | *A name for a person | A colour | A place | An action word
exercise: Why does Cyril start with a capital letter? | It is a colour | It is an action word | *It is a name, so it is a proper noun | It is a place on a map
exercise: Which brother worked with Saint Cyril to bring writing to the Slavic peoples? | Cyrus | Patrick | *Methodius | Peter
test: «Great-grandad was called Cyril, and it was a popular name in the early 1900s.» When was Cyril popular in Britain? | The year 2050 | 1600s | *The early 1900s | Today only
test: «Saint Cyril was a Christian missionary of the 800s.» In which century did Saint Cyril live? | The 1300s | The 1000s | The 1800s | *The 800s
exam: «The Cyrillic alphabet is named after Saint Cyril, though his followers probably made it.» Who is the Cyrillic alphabet named after? | Methodius | Cyril the king | Cyrus | *Saint Cyril
